@namespace Lumeo.Docs.Shared.Showcases

@* Overlay (OverlayService/OverlayProvider) is a low-level DI service with no visual identity
   of its own — it has no `<Overlay>` primitive to render; calling it opens a real Dialog/Sheet
   at the app's root-mounted OverlayProvider, which would take over the whole page from inside a
   catalog card. Per the README's exception pattern this renders a faithful static rendition of
   what OverlayService.ShowConfirmAsync produces: a Dialog-shaped panel (it renders through
   Dialog/DialogContent under the hood), triggered by the same "Open a Dialog" button as the
   component's own docs page. *@
<div class="w-full max-w-[22rem]">
    <Stack Gap="2">
        <Button Size="Button.ButtonSize.Sm" Class="w-fit">Open Dialog</Button>
        <Stack Gap="2" Class="rounded-lg border border-border/40 bg-background p-3 shadow-lg">
            <Lumeo.Text Size="sm" Weight="semibold">Confirm</Lumeo.Text>
            <Lumeo.Text Size="xs" Color="muted">Opened programmatically via OverlayService — no local open/closed state to manage.</Lumeo.Text>
        </Stack>
    </Stack>
</div>
